Events](/event-calendar)\n  + [Social Media](/social-media)\n  + [Broadcast Media](/video/broadcast-media)\n  + [Image Gallery](/image-gallery)\n  + [Videos](/video)\n  + [Press Resources](/press-resources)\n* About  \n  NHGRI\n\n  [About  \n  NHGRI](/about-nhgri)+ [Organization](/about-nhgri/Organization)\n  + [Mission and Vision](/about-nhgri/NHGRI-Vision-and-Mission)\n  + [Policies and Guidance](/about-nhgri/Policies-Guidance)\n  + [Budget](/about-nhgri/Budget-Financial-Information)\n  + [Institute Advisors](/about-nhgri/Institute-Advisors)\n  + [Strategic Vision](/2020SV)\n  + [Partner with NHGRI](/about-nhgri/Partner-with-NHGRI)\n  + [Staff Search](/staff)\n  + [Contact Us](/about-nhgri/Contact)\n\nBreadcrumb\n----------\n\n1. [Home](/)\n2. [About Genomics](/about-genomics)\n3. [Educational Resources](/About-Genomics/Educational-Resources)\n4. [Talking Glossary of Genomic and Genetic Terms](/node/41621)\n5. Polygenic Risk Score (PRS)\n\n[Home](/)\n\n[About Genomics](/about-genomics)\n\n[Educational Resources](/About-Genomics/Educational-Resources)\n\n[Talking Glossary of Genomic and Genetic Terms](/node/41621)\n\n[En Español](/es/genetics-glossary/Polygenic-Risk-Score)\n\n\n\n![NHGRI logo](/themes/custom/nhgri/assets/global/NHGRI_grey_teal.svg)\n\n![Polygenic Risk Scores](/sites/default/files/media/images/2022-05/Generic-PRS_hero.png)\n\nPolygenic Risk Score (PRS)\n==========================\n\nupdated: September 15, 2026\n\nDefinition\n----------\n\nA polygenic risk score (abbreviated PRS) uses genomic information alone to assess a person’s chances of having or developing a particular medical condition. A person’s PRS is a statistical calculation based on the presence or absence of multiple genomic variants, without taking environmental or other factors into account.\n\nNarration\n---------\n\nPolygenic risk score. We know the differences in how the spelling of a person's DNA or genomic variants interact with many other factors such as their health habits, the drugs they're taking, and the diseases they may develop. So polygenic risk scores, or PRS, are only one factor in predicting disease. Still, just because of the play of chance, there are some people who happen to have a large number of harmful variants that can put them at the top 1% or even the top 1/1,000 or 1/10,000 of risk. Such individuals may do better if they are tested more frequently for early signs of disease as with mammograms, for example, or if they adopt lifestyle changes early on to help prevent the disease entirely. As scientists learn more about using PRS, we may see such scores coming into wider use.\n\n![Teri Manolio](/sites/default/files/media/images/2021-06/manolio_teri.jpg)\n\n[Teri Manolio, M.D., Ph.D.](/staff/Teri-Manolio-MD-PhD)\n\nDirector\n\nDivision of Genomic Medicine\n\nSearch\n------\n\n[Back to Glossary](/genetics-glossary)\n\nRelated\n-------\n\n[![DNA](/sites/default/files/media/images/2022-04/DNA_dyn.png)](/genetics-glossary/Deoxyribonucleic-Acid-DNA)\n\n[Deoxyribonucleic Acid (DNA)](/genetics-glossary/Deoxyribonucleic-Acid-DNA)\n\n[![Generic DNA bases](/sites/default/files/media/images/2022-05/Generic-DNA-bases_dyn.jpg)](/genetics-glossary/Risk)\n\n[Risk](/genetics-glossary/Risk)\n\n[![DNA](/sites/default/files/media/images/2022-04/DNA_dyn.png)](/genetics-glossary/Genomic-Medicine)\n\n[Genomic Medicine](/genetics-glossary/Genomic-Medicine)\n\n[![Generic Bases](/sites/default/files/media/images/2022-04/Generic-Bases_dyn.jpg)](/genetics-glossary/Precision-Medicine)\n\n[Precision Medicine](/genetics-glossary/Precision-Medicine)\n\n\n\n### Get Updates\n\nEnter your email address to receive updates about the latest advances in genomics research.\n\nSubscribe!\n\n### Social Media Stream\n\nFooter Links\n------------\n\n* [Contact](/about-nhgri/Contact)\n* [Accessibility](/about-nhgri/Policies-Guidance/Accessibility)\n* [Site Map](/about-nhgri/Policies-Guidance/Site-Map)\n* [Staff Search](/staff)\n* [Plug-Ins Used by HHS](https://www.hhs.gov/web/policies-and-standards/hhs-web-policies/plugins/index.html \"Plug-Ins Used by HHS (External Link)\")\n* [FOIA](https://www.nih.gov/institutes-nih/nih-office-director/office-communications-public-liaison/freedom-information-act-office)\n* [Privacy](/about-nhgri/Policies-Guidance/Privacy)\n* [Copyright](/about-nhgri/Policies-Guidance/Copyright)\n* [HHS Vulnerability Disclosure](https://www.hhs.gov/vulnerability-disclosure-policy/index.html \"Vulnerability Disclosure Policy (External Link)\")\n\n---\n",
