3%A8re) [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&num=10&btnG=Search+Scholar&as_epq=&as_oq=&as_eq=&as_occt=any&as_sauthors=%22Jean-Philippe%20Laverdi%C3%A8re%22&as_publication=&as_ylo=&as_yhi=&as_allsubj=all&hl=en)\n5. Simon Nadeau\n\n   [View author publications](/search?author=Simon%20Nadeau)\n\n   Search author on:[PubMed](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&term=Simon%20Nadeau) [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&num=10&btnG=Search+Scholar&as_epq=&as_oq=&as_eq=&as_occt=any&as_sauthors=%22Simon%20Nadeau%22&as_publication=&as_ylo=&as_yhi=&as_allsubj=all&hl=en)\n6. France Gagnon\n\n   [View author publications](/search?author=France%20Gagnon)\n\n   Search author on:[PubMed](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&term=France%20Gagnon) [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&num=10&btnG=Search+Scholar&as_epq=&as_oq=&as_eq=&as_occt=any&as_sauthors=%22France%20Gagnon%22&as_publication=&as_ylo=&as_yhi=&as_allsubj=all&hl=en)\n7. Funda Ogut\n\n   [View author publications](/search?author=Funda%20Ogut)\n\n   Search author on:[PubMed](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&term=Funda%20Ogut) [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&num=10&btnG=Search+Scholar&as_epq=&as_oq=&as_eq=&as_occt=any&as_sauthors=%22Funda%20Ogut%22&as_publication=&as_ylo=&as_yhi=&as_allsubj=all&hl=en)\n8. Harry X. Wu\n\n   [View author publications](/search?author=Harry%20X.%20Wu)\n\n   Search author on:[PubMed](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&term=Harry%20X.%20Wu) [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&num=10&btnG=Search+Scholar&as_epq=&as_oq=&as_eq=&as_occt=any&as_sauthors=%22Harry%20X.%20Wu%22&as_publication=&as_ylo=&as_yhi=&as_allsubj=all&hl=en)\n9. Martin Perron\n\n   [View author publications](/search?author=Martin%20Perron)\n\n   Search author on:[PubMed](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&term=Martin%20Perron) [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&num=10&btnG=Search+Scholar&as_epq=&as_oq=&as_eq=&as_occt=any&as_sauthors=%22Martin%20Perron%22&as_publication=&as_ylo=&as_yhi=&as_allsubj=all&hl=en)\n10. Jean Bousquet\n\n    [View author publications](/search?author=Jean%20Bousquet)\n\n    Search author on:[PubMed](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=search&term=Jean%20Bousquet) [Google Scholar](https://scholar.google.co.uk/scholar?as_q=&num=10&btnG=Search+Scholar&as_epq=&as_oq=&as_eq=&as_occt=any&as_sauthors=%22Jean%20Bousquet%22&as_publication=&as_ylo=&as_yhi=&as_allsubj=all&hl=en)\n\n### Contributions\n\nAS assisted in designing the study, curated and analysed the data, conducted analyses, and prepared the original draft of the manuscript. JBo, PL, and JBe contributed to conceptualization, study design, investigation, validation, supervision, funding support, and manuscript writing and review. J-PL and SN contributed to data analysis and manuscript review. FG handled the new raw genotyping data for black spruce and white spruce and validation of their quality, also contributing to manuscript review. FO contributed to funding support and manuscript review. HW and MP provided data for Norway spruce and black spruce, respectively, as well as manuscript review.\n\n### Corresponding authors\n\nCorrespondence to\n[André Soro](mailto:dogninema-andre.soro.1@ulaval.ca) or [Jean Bousquet](mailto:jean.bousquet@sbf.ulaval.ca).\n\nEthics declarations\n-------------------\n\n### Competing interests\n\nThe authors declare no competing interests.\n\nAdditional information\n----------------------\n\n**Publisher’s note** Springer Nature remains neutral with regard to jurisdictional claims in published maps and institutional affiliations.\n\nAssociate editor: Pår Ingvarsson.\n\nSupplementary information\n-------------------------\n\n### [Supplementary Material (download PDF )](https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-stat